hadiths[9]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27814","Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his mother Umm Kulthum, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: He is not a liar who says something from a man seeking to reconcile between people."
"27815","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, he said: Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Ubaydillah ibn Shihab narrated to us that Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf informed him that his mother Umm Kulthum bint Uqbah informed him that she heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The liar is not the one who reconciles between people, conveying good or saying good."
"27816","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his mother Umm Kulthum bint Uqbah, and she was among the first emigrant women, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The liar is not the one who reconciles between people, saying good or conveying good. And he said once: conveying good."
"27817","Umayyah ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Muslim, the nephew of al-Zuhri, narrated to us, from his uncle al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his mother, that she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Say: He is Allah, the One, equals a third of the Qur'an."
"27818","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Layth, meaning Ibn Sa'd, narrated to us, from Yazid, meaning Ibn al-Had, from Abd al-Wahhab, from Ibn Shihab, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from his mother Umm Kulthum bint Uqbah, she said: I did not hear the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, permit anything of lying except in three: a man saying a statement intending thereby reconciliation, a man saying a statement in war, and a man speaking to his wife and a woman speaking to her husband."
"27819","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Khalid informed us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from his mother Umm Kulthum. My father said: And Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Muslim narrated to us, and he mentioned it, and he said: From his mother Umm Kulthum bint Abi Salamah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, married Umm Salamah, he said to her: I have sent to the Negus a robe and measures of musk, and I do not think the Negus but has died, and I do not think but that my gift will be returned to me, so if it is returned to me it is for you. She said: And it was as the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, and his gift was returned to him, so he gave every woman among his wives an ounce of musk, and he gave Umm Salamah the rest of the musk and the robe."
"27820","Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his mother Umm Kulthum bint Uqbah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The liar is not the one who reconciles between people, saying good or conveying good."
"27821","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from his mother Umm Kulthum bint Uqbah, that she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, permitted lying in three: in war, in reconciling between people, and a man's speech to his wife."
"27822","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf narrated to me, from his mother Umm Kulthum bint Uqbah, he said: And she was among the first emigrant women, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: He is not a liar who reconciles between people, saying good or conveying good. And he said once: conveying good."
